    "body": "@Ashwinsuriya The stale-pass cases are exactly the kind of failure I've been investigating.\n\nOne thing I find especially interesting is that a successful test run isn't necessarily evidence of completion if the source changed afterward. And a narrowed run shouldn't count as proof that the full suite passed.\n\nI've been building an experimental completion verifier called Truth Firewall, but it currently checks declared conditions against the current state — it doesn't yet handle historical Claude session records.\n\nWould you be open to sharing one small sanitized stale-pass case? I'd be interested in testing the boundary against an actual failure instead of another case I invented myself.",
