    "updated_at": "2026-11-06T15:22:16Z",
    "body": "The tail finding is the big one. Put set -o pipefail in front of any test command the agent runs, and ask it to paste the summary line and echo $? in the same message as the claim. For stale passes, ask for the run time and the last-edit time. A run older than the edit is no pass. I built Andon (free, open source), a Stop hook whose opt-in mode refuses a piped run without pipefail. It still credits a run from before the last edit. https://github.com/PrimeFoldTools/Andon",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
