    "created_at": "2026-11-07T12:04:16Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-11-07T12:04:16Z",
    "body": "The stale pass is the one I run into most too. Claude runs the tests, they pass, it makes one more edit, then says \"all tests pass\" without running them again.\n\nAdding a line to CLAUDE.md helped a bit (rerun if you touched any file since the last test run, and say which tests you ran if it was only some of them). It still forgets sometimes though.\n\nSo I wrote a Stop hook for it, called honestly (I'm the author, it's MIT, plain Python, no model calls). Before the reply goes out it checks whether tests actually ran after the last edit and what the summary line says, so `npm test | tail` printing \"1 failed\" gets caught even though the exit code is 0. It also blocks pipes like `| head` or `| grep -c` that hide the summary from Claude in the first place.\n\nOn my own sessions from the last 60 days it held 12 replies, and 11 of those really had nothing behind them.\n\nhttps://github.com/kennywu411-dev/honestly\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
